WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.668
A new documentary has shed new light

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.603
on a fleet of Russian ghost ships

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.772
gathering intelligence in the North Sea.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.373
The investigation

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.607
by four public broadcasters

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.509
from four Nordic countries

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.710
say the ships have used

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.978
underwater surveillance equipment

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.380
to map key sites.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.381
Those include military

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.315
training areas, oil

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.850
and gas fields, airports

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.284
and even windfarms.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:18.885
The broadcaster

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:19.652
say some of the ships

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.755
identify themselves as research vessels

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.223
or fishing trawlers.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.891
But the reports say that route suggests

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.860
they're up to something else entirely.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.261
The Kremlin's chief spokesperson

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:32.132
is calling the accusations baseless

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:32.766
Well, Steve

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.833
Hall is a CNN

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:34.501
national security

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.535
analyst and former chief

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.803
of Russia operations

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.204
for the CIA. Steve,

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.639
thanks for being with us.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.007
Great to be here.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:41.741
So in February,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.743
Dutch military intelligence reported

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.378
a Russian ship was detected

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.146
near an offshore

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.814
wind farm and was escorted

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.615
out of the North Sea

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.649
by the Dutch Coast Guard,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.383
with officials

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.317
later warning

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.719
Russia is secretly charting

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.820
this infrastructure

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.055
and is undertaking activities

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.689
which indicate preparations

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.958
for disruption and sabotage.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.561
And a few months before that, a southern

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.497
defense analyst tweeted this.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.299
If you live on the East Coast of Scotland

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.101
and you look out your window today,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.502
you might see the Russian spy

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.270
ship, Admiral

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.372
Vladimir Ski, heading south.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.640
It's been known for a while

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.641
that Russian ships

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.909
often described as research

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.410
vessels or fishing trawlers

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.812
have been mapping the location of,

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.112
you know,

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.880
critical maritime infrastructure.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.182
It seems this new information,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.149
which is our public,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.317
is about the extent

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.419
of that spying operation, in particular

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.521
the number of Russian ships involved.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.989
So what more do we know at this point?

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.259
Well, you know, what we

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.360
what we know at this point,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.396
I think, is sort of a reinforcement

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.264
or simply an escalation

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:38.832
of what really

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.000
has been going on for decades.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.001
The Russians

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.536
certainly since Vladimir Putin took over,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.405
but probably before then as well,

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.773
have always been very active

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:47.373
and very active

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.408
in the Baltic region,

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.642
especially in the Baltic

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.544
Maritime situation,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.812
because it's key

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.379
to how

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.381
they viewed their defensive posture.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.150
And now that NATO's has enlarged,

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.318
notably Finland,

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.787
which has increased the land border

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:01.921
we can't forget

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.589
because a lot of people spent

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.157
a lot of time looking at land maps.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.758
There is a huge ocean map,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.193
of course, that the Russians

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.595
have to be concerned about,

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.897
as do NATO's allies, new or old,

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.765
because of the huge coastlines

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.466
that they have.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.567
So this is actually something

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.002
that's been going on for a long time.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.237
But the new pieces

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.439
now, we're seeing exactly how large

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.441
this new effort is to collect

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.509
that sort of intelligence

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.710
that the Russians believe

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.477
that they need

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.311
because of the threat

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.913
that they feel from NATO's.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.448
It's also coming in the background

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.816
of the war in Ukraine.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:30.817
So how does that play to this?

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.386
Can we expect some kind of Russian attack

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.821
on these maritime assets?

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.589
What this is, is preparation,

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.857
because they understand

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.558
that they might have to

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.192
there might be a time

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.493
when they have to either fight

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.828
to protect themselves or push back

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.396
or at least that's what they believe.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.697
There's also a propaganda

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.498
angle to this, John,

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.000
and that is that the Russians

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.601
want to say, well, what did you expect?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.035
Of course,

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:49.936
if NATO's going to act

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.971
recklessly and threaten Russia,

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:52.205
you know,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.339
we have to protect our interests.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:53.840
Of course,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.141
NATO's a defensive alliance

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:55.942
and has no intention

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.410
of doing anything against Russia

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.778
unless Russia attacks first

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.879
but they have to be prepared,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.380
the Russians

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.549
do, for any eventuality that they think

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.150
they think could happen

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.151
in this joint investigation

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.152
by public broadcasters

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.620
from four Nordic countries

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.389
track that the aforementioned vessel,

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.890
the Admiral Vladimir Ski,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.393
which was approached by journalists

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.495
from these four broadcasters.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.197
This is what happened in that instance.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:17.964
Here it is.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.265
We're filming everything on the ship

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.733
and filming in tennis.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.202
As we've been told by the source.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:23.636
I can

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.271
see crew members

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.540
walking around on the deck.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.242
I think they're watching us.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.344
There's two men staring at us

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.414
while they're looking at us.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.783
This is really a strange situation,

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.151
almost a tense situation.

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.285
They're looking at us

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.720
even though this ship had disabled

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.522
its locator beacon.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.224
It appears that the Muskie

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.059
had been approaching wind farms.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.260
And as it did, it slowed down

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.795
and loitered in the area.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.262
And according

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.164
to the Norwegian Broadcasting

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:51.497
Company,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.499
that all of these Russian vessels

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.168
have been sailing past military training

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.103
areas, important oil and gas fields

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:57.837
small airports,

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:58.738
deep water keys

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.206
and strategically important hubs

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.041
for the Norwegian armed forces.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.343
So what intelligence

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.411
are they actually being able to get here?

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.512
How would that intelligence

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.647
be used by Russia?

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.349
And how vulnerable are these sites?

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:11.851
So this is a

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.753
this is an intelligence

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.421
bonanza, I think for for

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.657
Russia is the best way to say it.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.559
The Russians are looking at

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.927
potential targets

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.096
that they would consider attacking

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.698
perhaps as part of their their philosophy

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.534
of of not necessarily direct warfare,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.936
but hybrid warfare.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.670
So, you know,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.105
we've seen strange things happen

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.173
beneath the surface of the Baltics.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.508
You know, recently there was

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.309
there was the pipeline

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.777
that somehow was was blown up.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.911
We still don't have at least

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.480
publicly don't understand

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.581
exactly how that happened.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.482
But the Russians

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.284
see great value in targets

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.286
such as gas pipelines.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.421
Some of these huge communication cables

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.356
that go across the Atlantic,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.258
which carry critical information

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.426
not just for the functioning

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.060
of our society,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.295
but for the functioning of

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.362
of the military

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.131
as well, of the wind farms.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:58.898
People might be saying,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.066
well, what about a wind farm?

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.267
But when you think about it,

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.202
that's essentially infrastructure.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.871
And if it's energy infrastructure

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:05.672
that we're talking about,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.172
the Russians

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.573
are going to be very interested

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.575
to know how they can make life difficult

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:10.977
for the West

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.779
if they go after some of these targets.

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.546
So all of

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.914
that is valuable

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.983
and viable collection information

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.484
that the Russians really need

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.385
if they want to conduct

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.454
some sort of hybrid warfare

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.822
that they can later deny

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.456
so that they don't

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.591
feel the full wrath of NATO's or the West

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.293
in the military fashion against them.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.161
There's a lot there for them

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.462
that they're that they want to collect

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.063
and are interested

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.497
in these ghost ships

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:31.931
they call them,

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.166
which are floating around

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:33.900
without their, like,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.268
locator beacons on

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:35.702
you know,

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.636
essentially everyone to see,

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:37.370
which is quite interesting

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.338
in all of this sea,

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.072
I think is being with us.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:39.739
We really appreciate it.

